Package: ubuntu-deep-uninstaller
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends},
 dpkg, apt, libgtk-4-1, libadwaita-1-0,
 policykit-1 | sudo
Recommends: flatpak, snapd, wine, ptyxis | gnome-terminal
Description: Deep, evidence-based application uninstaller for GNOME
 Detects whether an installed application came from APT, Flatpak, Snap,
 Wine, an AppImage, or a manual installation, and performs a careful,
 confirmed, best-effort removal of the application and its associated
 configuration, cache, and data. Integrates an "Uninstall Completely"
 action into the GNOME application grid's right-click menu.
 .
 Every destructive operation runs in a visible terminal with sudo
 requested interactively when needed; nothing is deleted without an
 explicit, itemized removal plan and confirmation.
